---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Submitting evidence for review — apprenti.dev Docs">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold">
                Submitting evidence for review
            </h1>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">
            <section>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    A submission is how a mentor reviews your work without
                    guessing. It bundles what you did, proof they can
                    inspect, and an honest account of any AI involvement.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    Evidence types
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    A task's evidence requirement can point at any of:
                </p>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-2">
                    <strong>repository</strong>, <strong>commit</strong>,
                    <strong>tag</strong>, <strong>url</strong>,
                    <strong>markdown</strong>,
                    <strong>file reference</strong>,
                    <strong>screenshot reference</strong>,
                    <strong>test result</strong>, <strong>benchmark</strong>,
                    <strong>demo</strong>, or <strong>other</strong>.
                </p>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    Whatever the type, evidence should be something a
                    mentor can actually open — a commit, a repository, a
                    test run, a specific file — not a claim. As the in-app
                    help puts it: <em>"I did it" is not evidence.</em>
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    Before you can submit
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    <strong>Submit for review</strong> stays disabled until
                    three things are complete:
                </p>
                <ol
                    class="space-y-3 text-muted-foreground mt-2 list-decimal pl-5"
                >
                    <li>
                        <strong>Reflection</strong> — at least 20 characters
                        answering what you tried and what's still unclear.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Evidence note</strong> — at least 8
                        characters pointing at something inspectable: a
                        commit, a repository path, a conflict-resolution
                        note, a test run.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>AI disclosure</strong> — required whenever
                        the task's policy asks for it. Choose one:
                        <ul class="space-y-1 text-muted-foreground mt-2">
                            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                                <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span
                                ><strong>None</strong> — you did not use AI
                                on this task.
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                                <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span
                                ><strong>Assisted</strong> — AI explained a
                                concept, asked a Socratic question, or gave
                                a hint; you wrote the notes, code, and
                                evidence.
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                                <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span
                                ><strong>Generated</strong> — AI produced
                                substantial wording or code that you adapted
                                into the submission.
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    Leaving disclosure blank is not the same as choosing
                    <strong>None</strong> — pick deliberately. If a task has
                    AI-sourced notes attached but disclosure is still
                    <strong>None</strong>, the app warns you (it will still
                    let you submit if the task's policy allows that
                    combination) rather than silently rewriting your
                    answer.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    What happens after Submit
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Your submission becomes a durable, structured record in
                    your fork, visible to your mentor once they sync. From
                    there, a submission moves through: submitted →
                    approved, or submitted → revision requested →
                    resubmitted → approved (or revision requested again).
                </p>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    If your mentor requests a revision, you'll see their
                    comment on the task, make the change, and resubmit —
                    the history of every round trip stays attached to the
                    task, not just the latest attempt.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 flex gap-4">
            <a href="/docs" class="text-sm text-link hover:underline"
                >← All Docs</a
            >
            <a href="/" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:underline"
                >Back to apprenti.dev</a
            >
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
